findings.body:
After `navigator.performAction(Action.SelectLightTheme)`, the test now reads `app.buttons[...Appearance.darkThemeView].value` and assigns it to `lightIsSelected`. It then expects `"1"`. Once Light is selected, the Dark button should be `"0"`, so this assertion fails. The test is now broken, and it no longer checks the light theme at all.

The change also doesn't match the PR description, which says the test was rebuilt to match new steps. The diff only changes the identifier and the TestRail link.

::diff{file="firefox-ios/firefox-ios-tests/Tests/XCUITests/DisplaySettingsTests.swift" lines="46-54"}

::suggestion{file="firefox-ios/firefox-ios-tests/Tests/XCUITests/DisplaySettingsTests.swift" lines="53-54"}
let lightIsSelected = app.buttons[AccessibilityIdentifiers.Settings.Appearance.lightThemeView].value
XCTAssertEqual(lightIsSelected as? String, "1")

Three helpers in `ClipBoardTests` are changed to `public func`, but nothing outside this class calls them, and other test helpers in this suite aren't declared `public`. The change adds noise without a reason.

Removing the `checkCopiedUrl()` call from `testClipboard` also leaves `checkCopiedUrl` with no callers. Its only remaining reference is inside the commented-out `testClipboardPasteAndGo` block. That makes it dead code. Either remove it or keep the call that uses it.

::diff{file="firefox-ios/firefox-ios-tests/Tests/XCUITests/ClipBoardTests.swift" lines="8-12"}
